# Code owners for Perihelion Protocol
# These owners are requested for review automatically when matching files change.
# Replace the placeholder team/handles with real maintainers as the org grows.
#
# IMPORTANT: Rules are evaluated last-match-wins (bottom entries take precedence
# over top entries for the same path), so security-sensitive path overrides are
# listed AFTER the broad package rules that they supersede.
#
# Review policy for security-sensitive paths is documented in CONTRIBUTING.md
# and SECURITY.md. Branch protection MUST require CODEOWNERS review
# (Settings → Branches → Require review from Code Owners) for these rules to
# be enforced on PRs.

# ── Default: org maintainers own everything not otherwise specified ──────────
*                                                   @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers

# ── TypeScript packages ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/sdk/                                               @Perihelion-Protocol/ts-maintainers
/solver/                                            @Perihelion-Protocol/ts-maintainers
/relayer/                                           @Perihelion-Protocol/ts-maintainers
/mempool/                                           @Perihelion-Protocol/ts-maintainers

# ── Soroban (Rust) contracts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/contracts/soroban/                                 @Perihelion-Protocol/soroban-maintainers

# ── EVM (Solidity) contracts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/contracts/evm/                                     @Perihelion-Protocol/evm-maintainers

# ── Shared cross-chain artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/contracts/shared/                                  @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers

# ── Documentation & specifications ───────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/                                              @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers

# ── CI/CD workflows ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.github/workflows/                                 @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers

# ── Security-sensitive meta files ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/SECURITY.md                                        @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers
/.github/                                           @Perihelion-Protocol/maintainers

# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECURITY-SENSITIVE PATHS — require @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers
#
# These files contain fund-moving logic, cryptographic primitives, replay
# guards, and cross-chain wire formats. A subtle change to any of them could
# allow loss of user funds, double-settlement, or signature forgery. They
# require at least one approval from the security-designated team in addition
# to the package owner review. See CONTRIBUTING.md §Security review policy.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Wire codec — cross-chain message encoding/decoding (Soroban side).
# Malformed or inconsistent encoding breaks I5 (hash stability) and can
# allow the EVM and Soroban contracts to disagree on intent identity.
/contracts/soroban/settlement/src/messages.rs       @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# Core Soroban settlement logic — fill_intent, cancel_expired_intent,
# lz_receive, nonce/replay guard (InboundNonceBitmap), and all storage
# mutations that affect Locked/Filled/ConfirmationSent/Cancelled state.
/contracts/soroban/settlement/src/lib.rs            @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# Soroban type definitions — IntentStatus enum, DataKey variants, and
# the cancel-reason taxonomy shared with the EVM side.
/contracts/soroban/settlement/src/types.rs          @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# EVM escrow — lock(), lzReceive() (_onFillConfirmed/_onCancelIntent),
# cancelExpired(): all fund-moving paths. Also holds EIP-712 domain,
# INTENT_TYPEHASH, and the reentrancy mutex.
/contracts/evm/src/PerihelionEscrow.sol             @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# EVM timelock — governs all privileged admin operations (setPeer,
# setConfirmationGrace, guardian management). Changes here affect the
# trust/upgrade model of the entire protocol.
/contracts/evm/src/PerihelionTimelock.sol           @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# Shared wire-format test vectors — ground truth for codec differential
# fuzzing. Tampering with these vectors can mask encoder/decoder divergence
# between the Soroban and EVM sides.
/contracts/shared/                                  @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# SDK intent hashing — hashIntent() and INTENT_TYPEHASH/PERIHELION_DOMAIN
# must stay byte-identical to the EVM escrow (Invariant I5). Changes break
# the universal intent_hash across all components.
/sdk/src/intent.ts                                  @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# SDK type definitions — IntentStatus lifecycle vocabulary and the Intent
# interface; changes can desync the SDK from on-chain state machines.
/sdk/src/types.ts                                   @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# SDK intent validation — the pre-signature checks (minDestAmount, deadline,
# destination/destAsset shape) that stand between a malformed or economically
# unsound intent and a user's signature. Weakening a check here has the same
# blast radius as a contract-side validation bug.
/sdk/src/validate.ts                                @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers

# CI/CD workflows — a change that weakens a required check, disables a gate,
# or grants broader permissions to a workflow is a security change, not a
# routine CI edit. (An admin merge bypassing a required check is how the
# refund-helper regression reached main; see CONTRIBUTING.md.) This overrides
# the broader `@maintainers` rule above for the same path.
/.github/workflows/                                 @Perihelion-Protocol/security-reviewers
